There is no TypeScript module augmentation for the custom matcher. Without a declaration like:
```ts
declare module 'vitest' {
  interface Assertion<R = any> {
    toHaveLiveRegion(options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions): R;
  }
}
```
(and a parallel one for `@storybook/test` if needed), callers writing `expect(el).toHaveLiveRegion(...)` will get a TypeScript error such as `Property 'toHaveLiveRegion' does not exist on type 'Assertion'`. The runtime call works after `expect.extend`, but TypeScript will flag every usage site as a type error in strict projects.
